{
  "summary": "The screen reads as one long unscaled block: the display-size title eats a third of the viewport, body copy is oversized with loose leading, and the Accept CTA floats in the middle with ~400px of dead space beneath it. Tightening the type scale in the theme, moving the checkbox + Accept into a sticky footer inside a shared Screen scaffold, and giving the policy card a proper MD3 surface treatment would fix this screen and carry to every other screen.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Screen title \"Terms of Use and Privacy Policy\"",
      "issue": "Rendered at display size (~44px) so it wraps to two lines and consumes 180px before any content; the subtitle below it is nearly body-large, so hierarchy is only size, not weight/colour.",
      "fix": "Use `<Text variant=\"headlineMedium\">` (28/36, weight 600) for the title and `<Text variant=\"bodyMedium\" style={{color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant}}>` for \"Version 1. Please read and agree to continue.\" with 8px gap between them and 24px below. Cap headline/display fontSize in theme.ts fonts so no screen uses >28px at phone width.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Page layout / Accept CTA placement",
      "issue": "Everything is stacked top-aligned in a single scroll view, leaving ~400px empty below the CTA on phone and ~250px on desktop; the primary action is not anchored and can be pushed off-screen when policy text grows.",
      "fix": "Make the policy card area `flex: 1` inside a `ScrollView contentContainerStyle={{paddingBottom: 16}}`, and put the checkbox + Accept button + helper text in a fixed footer `View` with `padding: 24`, `borderTopWidth: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth`, `borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant`, `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface`. Implement as the shared `Screen` component's `footer` prop so forms (Save receipt/mileage) reuse it.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Agreement checkbox row",
      "issue": "Bare `Checkbox` next to a `Text`: the label is not tappable, the box is top-aligned against a two-line label, and the hit area is under 48px.",
      "fix": "Replace with `<Checkbox.Item label=\"I have read and agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy.\" status={checked ? 'checked' : 'unchecked'} position=\"leading\" mode=\"android\" labelVariant=\"bodyMedium\" labelStyle={{textAlign:'left'}} style={{paddingHorizontal:0, minHeight:48}} onPress={toggle} />` so the whole row toggles and the label aligns to the control.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Policy card body text",
      "issue": "Section bodies render at ~17px with ~40px line height, so three short paragraphs fill a whole phone screen and feel like a legal wall.",
      "fix": "Set section headings to `titleSmall` (14/20, weight 600) and body to `bodyMedium` with `lineHeight: 20` via theme.fonts; spacing: 8px between heading and its paragraph, 16px between sections. Card padding 16px (Card.Content default) instead of the current ~32px.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Policy card container",
      "issue": "1px outlined card on a near-identical background reads flat and the 16px+ radius plus thick border looks dated against MD3 surfaces.",
      "fix": "Use `<Card mode=\"contained\">` with `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surfaceContainerLow` (or surfaceVariant), `borderRadius: 12`, no border; keep the scroll fade by giving the ScrollView `showsVerticalScrollIndicator`. Define this as the default `AppCard` in src/components/ui/.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Accept button + \"Tick the box above to continue.\" helper",
      "issue": "Disabled button is full-width but visually dead, and the helper is a centred grey caption floating with no relationship to it; height of the button (~90px) is oversized.",
      "fix": "`<Button mode=\"contained\" disabled={!checked} style={{borderRadius: 8}} contentStyle={{height: 48}} labelStyle={{fontSize: 16}}>Accept</Button>` with the hint as `<HelperText type=\"info\" visible={!checked} style={{textAlign:'center'}}>` directly under it (4px gap), hidden once checked.",
      "shared": false
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The screen reads as a bare list: the primary 'add receipt' action promised by the spec is missing, the tab labels are clipped by the home-indicator area, and the ReceiptCard has no typographic hierarchy (amount, date, category and note are all nearly the same size and weight). Fixing the card and the tab bar in shared components lifts every list screen at once.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar (shared navigator / BottomNavigation)",
      "issue": "Labels 'Dashboard / Receipts / Mileage / Settings' are cut off at the bottom edge — the bar has no safe-area inset and insufficient height.",
      "fix": "In the shared tab navigator use useSafeAreaInsets(): tabBarStyle = { height: 64 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: 8 + insets.bottom, borderTopWidth: 1, borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant, backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface }, tabBarLabelStyle = { ...theme.fonts.labelMedium, fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 16 }, tabBarIconSize 24. Wrap screens in SafeAreaView edges={['top']} only.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Add-receipt FAB",
      "issue": "Spec requires the + FAB on ReceiptsScreen (empty-state copy even says 'Tap the + button'), but no FAB is rendered in the loaded state.",
      "fix": "Add <FAB icon=\"plus\" label=\"Add receipt\" (extended) onPress={navigate('ReceiptEntry')} style={{ position:'absolute', right:16, bottom: 16 + tabBarHeight }} /> using useBottomTabBarHeight(); give the FlatList contentContainerStyle paddingBottom: 96 so the last card is never covered.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "ReceiptCard typography",
      "issue": "Amount, date, category and note are all rendered at roughly the same size/weight, so nothing anchors the row; 'Date:' and 'Category:' label prefixes add noise.",
      "fix": "In src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx: amount Text variant=\"titleLarge\" fontWeight 700 color onSurface; drop the 'Date:'/'Category:' prefixes and render one secondary line Text variant=\"bodySmall\" color onSurfaceVariant as '2026-10-09 · Supplies'; note Text variant=\"bodyMedium\" color onSurfaceVariant numberOfLines={2}. Vertical rhythm: 4px between amount and meta, 8px before note.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "'Expense' type indicator in ReceiptCard",
      "issue": "Type is plain body text in the top-right, visually competing with the amount and giving no scannable income/expense distinction.",
      "fix": "Replace with <Chip compact mode=\"flat\" textStyle={theme.fonts.labelSmall} style={{ backgroundColor: isExpense ? theme.colors.errorContainer : theme.colors.secondaryContainer }}>Expense</Chip>, aligned with alignItems:'center' in the header row.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen header 'Receipts' + list spacing",
      "issue": "Title is oversized and indented 48px on mobile while the card sits at 16px, so the left edges don't align; list items have no defined gap for multiple rows.",
      "fix": "Create src/components/ui/ScreenHeader.tsx: Text variant=\"headlineMedium\" with paddingHorizontal:16, paddingTop:8, paddingBottom:16. FlatList contentContainerStyle={{ paddingHorizontal:16, gap:12 }} and Card mode=\"elevated\" elevation={1} with borderRadius 16 from theme.roundness.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Desktop (1280px) content column",
      "issue": "Content is centred in a ~512px column that leaves a huge empty field, and the tab bar stretches edge-to-edge, so the page feels unfinished.",
